    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald is delighted to present 'Hadleigh', a most attractive double fronted detached family home providing bright and nicely appointed accommodation extending to 218 sq.m (2,346 sq.ft) approx. It provides a wonderful balance of living and bedroom spaces that any growing family could require, complemented by generous southwest facing gardens.\n\nThis lovely home has been very well maintained over the years and there is a great sense of space and light throughout. The ground floor comprises of a bright and spacious tiled entrance hall with a cosy living room to the front of the house whilst a superbly spacious drawing / dining room opens out to the back garden. It also leads to a modern family / sunroom extension, built approx. 10 years ago, providing stunning light filled accommodation with floor to ceiling windows and doors overlooking the southwest facing gardens. A well-equipped kitchen and guest w.c. complete the accommodation at this level. Upstairs there are four fine bedrooms with one being ensuite and a large family bathroom. \n\nThe back garden benefits from an ideal southwest facing orientation and is laid out mainly in lawn with a selection of mature plants and trees. A large patio area is ideal for 'al fresco' dining. The front garden is enhanced by generous off-street parking and a garage to the side.\n\nThe property enjoys one of Donnybrook's most convenient locations, being within easy reach of an extensive selection of amenities. Just some of these amenities include: UCD Belfield, St. Vincent's Private & Public Hospitals, Elm Park Golf Course, and many of Dublin's premier secondary schools such as St. Michael's College, the Teresian School, Muckross Park, Blackrock College and St. Andrew's College. The property also benefits from being within easy reach of the excellent shopping facilities of Merrion Shopping Centre and Donnybrook. The city's principal business headquarters located on Merrion Square, St Stephens Green and Fitzwilliam Square are within a 10-minute drive. Dublin Airport is a 20-minute drive via the port tunnel."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hallway: - \nbright and spacious hall with attractive part panelled walls, tiled floor and cloakroom.\n\nGuest w.c.: - \nw.c and wash hand basin, part panelled walls and tiled floor.\n\nDrawing/Dining Room: - \nsuperb reception rooms with ceiling coving, attractive fireplace with coal effect gas fire. Doors to patio and garden.\n\nFamily/Sunroom: - \nmodern open plan family/sunroom suitable for everyday living and dining. Overlooking the private sunny garden. Attractive wooden flooring, velux windows, recessed lighting and built in display cabinets.\n\nLiving Room: - \nspacious reception room with attractive fireplace and coal effect gas fire, ceiling coving and lovely bay window.\n\nKitchen: - \nwith built in wall and floor presses. Integrated oven, hob, extractor fan, fridge freezer. Plumbed for dishwasher, panelled ceiling and recessed lighting.\n\nUPSTAIRS - \n\n\nLanding: - \nBright and spacious landing with part panelled walls and hotpress with good storage.\n\nMain Bedroom: - \nsuperb double room overlooking the back garden with built in wardrobes and dressing table.\n\nEnsuite Shower Room: - \nwith corner shower cubicle, w.c. and wash hand basin with underneath storage presses. Part panelled walls, tiled floor and recessed lighting.\n\nBedroom 2: - \nsuperb bright and exceptionally spacious double bedroom with built in wardrobes and overhead presses.\n\nBedroom 3: - \nwith built in desk.\n\nBedroom 4: - \nsuperb bright room with built in wardrobes and overhead presses. Attractive bay window.\n\nFamily Bathroom: - \nbath with shower attachment, w.c. and wash hand basin. Fully tiled walls and floor. Recessed lighting.\n\n"
      },
